I'll review this CLI slice read-only against the pinned upstream oracle, the round-2 inventory, and the port decisions, and report only new findings.Round 2 already closed several schema and runtime issues on these files. I'll read the binding decisions and the focused sources next, and only raise defects that are still open.The round-2 link fix still leaves a presence check in this slice. I'll probe that path, and the file-sink branch, against the schema the tests already accept.I'll verify the two candidate bugs against the current sources, the round-2 inventory, and the upstream oracle before numbering any findings.### fable-3-1
- file: scratchpad/effected/cli/CliLinks.ts:127
- class: bug   severity: required
- standard: EFFECTED_PORT_GOAL.md D11 (bug) and §14 (`upstream-bug`); `Doc.LinkTarget` executable contract. Closed `cli-r2-8` fixed only `internal/layout.ts` `safeTarget` and `Doc.link`'s default label.
- evidence: `scratchpad/test/cli/Doc.test.ts:417-420` asserts `S.is(LinkTarget)({ url: undefined, file: "src/a.ts", line: 3, col: 4 })` and that `Doc.link` labels with the file. `makeTarget` still branches on `"url" in target` and calls `cleanUrl(target.url)` (`CliLinks.ts:122`). `cleanUrl` calls `sanitize` (`Fmt.ts:59`), which calls `stripAnsi` (`internal/displayWidth.ts:29`: `input.replace`). `undefined.replace` throws `TypeError`. `CliLinks.layer` publishes this function as `target` (`CliLinks.ts:227`); `CliLinks.linker` calls `options.links.target(target)` before it can return the label (`CliLinks.ts:352`). The pinned oracle is the same check at `packages/cli/src/CliLinks.ts:82`. Layout paint already goes through `S.is(LinkTarget.members[0])` (`internal/layout.ts:57-63`), so this remaining crash is the public `target` / `linker` entry. No new runtime probe was run this round; the committed `S.is` assertion plus the `replace` chain is the evidence.
- failure: A schema-valid file link whose `url` key is `undefined` throws `TypeError` from `CliLinks.target` and from `linker` on a hyperlink-capable, non-agent stream, instead of resolving `file`.
- fix: Select the URL branch with `S.is(LinkTarget.members[0])`, then the existing file branch. A real string `url` still wins. Add a regression through `CliLinks.layerTest("file").target` and `linker` on the `Doc.test.ts` object, and record the verified upstream bug in the ledger and Port notes.

### fable-3-2
- file: scratchpad/effected/cli/CliLog.ts:650
- class: bug   severity: required
- standard: EFFECTED_PORT_GOAL.md D11 (bug) and §14 (`upstream-bug`); `CliLogFile` (`CliLog.ts:195-202`). Round-2 `cli-r2-5` kept path-over-envVar precedence for a real path string.
- evidence: `CliLogFile` is `S.Union` of an `envVar` struct then a `path` struct, the same `S.Struct` excess-key rule the green `Doc.test.ts:419` assertion pins: an extra `undefined` sibling key does not reject `S.is`, and TypeScript skips excess-property checks on the union, so `{ path: undefined, envVar: "TOOL_LOG" }` is a `CliLogFile`. `"path" in file` is true for that object, so the branch sets `O.some(undefined)`. `undefined !== ""`, and `Path.resolve` (`packages/effect/src/Path.ts:398` and `:413`) reads `path.length` and throws `TypeError`. The env var is never read. The pinned oracle is the same check at `packages/cli/src/CliLog.ts:508`. `S.is(CliLogFile)` on this object was not re-probed this round; it follows the committed `LinkTarget` excess-key result.
- failure: Building `CliLog.layer` with that file config dies while resolving the sink path, so a set `TOOL_LOG` never opens the file sink.
- fix: Take the path branch only with `S.is(CliLogFile.members[1])` (the path struct). A real string path still wins; `path: undefined` falls through to `Config.String(file.envVar)`. Add a layer regression and record the verified upstream bug in the ledger and Port notes.

